1. A method of manufacturing a pre-insulated pipe, the method comprising:

   providing an inner pipe having an outer surface;

   arranging a layer of thermally insulating material around the outer surface of the inner pipe to form an insulated inner pipe, the layer of thermally insulating material having an uncompressed outer diameter greater than an inner diameter of an outer jacket pipe;

   providing the outer jacket pipe having a pipe bore extending in a longitudinal direction;

   applying an overpressure to the insulated inner pipe, to a space surrounding the insulated inner pipe, or to an inlet region of the outer jacket pipe, such that the overpressure radially compresses the layer of thermally insulating material to reduce an effective outer diameter of the insulated inner pipe;

   while the layer of thermally insulating material is radially compressed by the overpressure, inserting the insulated inner pipe into the bore of the outer jacket pipe in the longitudinal direction; and

   reducing the overpressure after insertion such that the layer of thermally insulating material expands into contact with an inner surface of the outer jacket pipe, thereby forming the pre-insulated pipe.

1. A method for producing a pre-insulated pipe, the method comprising:

providing a guide channel having a front end and a rear end;

arranging a jacket pipe in or along the guide channel such that the jacket pipe extends in a longitudinal direction between the front end and the rear end of the guide channel;

providing insulated inner piping comprising at least one inner pipe surrounded by insulating material;

introducing the insulated inner piping into the jacket pipe from the rear end of the guide channel toward the front end of the guide channel; and

during the introducing of the insulated inner piping into the jacket pipe, applying an overpressure to the jacket pipe and/or to the guide channel so as to facilitate movement of the insulated inner piping through the jacket pipe.

1. A process for producing an insulated pipe assembly, comprising the steps of:

- fixing a jacket pipe in a guide channel;
- providing an inner pipe surrounded by a layer of compressible thermal insulation;
- introducing the inner pipe with the compressible thermal insulation into the jacket pipe; and
- pushing the inner pipe with the compressible thermal insulation through the jacket pipe,

characterised in that, during the pushing of the inner pipe through the jacket pipe, compressed air is supplied into the jacket pipe so as to generate an air pressure acting radially on the compressible thermal insulation, thereby radially compressing the insulation and reducing the frictional resistance between the insulation and the jacket pipe.
